				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Air): Implement daemon lifecycle management and health monitoring\n\nThis commit adds robust daemon lifecycle management and comprehensive health monitoring to the Air background service, enhancing its reliability as a critical component in the Land code editor ecosystem.\n\nThe changes introduce a new `DaemonManager` module that handles PID file management, singleton enforcement through daemon locking, and platform-specific service integration for Linux, macOS, and Windows. This ensures only one instance of the Air daemon runs at a time, preventing resource conflicts. Additionally, a `HealthCheckManager` module provides multi-level health monitoring for core services (authentication, updates, downloader, indexing, gRPC, and connections) with support for automatic recovery triggers based on failure thresholds and response times.\n\nIntegration into the main binary includes initializing these systems during boot, registering services for health monitoring, and spawning background tasks for continuous health checks. The shutdownsequence now includes proper daemon lock release and health statistics reporting. This foundation improves the operational stability of Air's background services, which support key Land infrastructure components like the Vine gRPC communication layer.",
